# Written for the VS Code REST Client extension: requests reuse the created task through `# @name`.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3001

### List tasks, newest first (status: all | active | completed)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tasks?status=all&limit=50&offset=0

### Create a task
# @name createTask
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Buy milk" }

### Get the created task; the ETag header carries its version
@taskId = {{createTask.response.body.id}}
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tasks/{{taskId}}

### Mark it done, only if nobody changed it since version 1
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tasks/{{taskId}}
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: "1"

{ "completed": true }

### Same If-Match again: the task is at version 2 now, so this answers 412
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tasks/{{taskId}}
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: "1"

{ "title": "Buy oat milk" }

### A weak ETag never matches: If-Match uses strong comparison, so this answers 412
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tasks/{{taskId}}
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: W/"2"

{ "title": "Buy oat milk" }

### A list of ETags matches when any of them is the current version
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tasks/{{taskId}}
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: "1", "2"

{ "title": "Buy oat milk" }

### Rename without a precondition (last write wins)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tasks/{{taskId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Buy oat milk" }

### Delete the task
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tasks/{{taskId}}

### An invalid title answers 400 with one entry per field
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "   " }
